values
('qq-4-001','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A student is reviewing bacterial shapes before an infection-control exam. Which pairing is correct?','Cocci—round; bacilli—rod-shaped; spirilla—spiral-shaped','Cocci—rod-shaped; bacilli—spiral-shaped; spirilla—round','Cocci—spiral-shaped; bacilli—round; spirilla—rod-shaped','Cocci—spore-forming; bacilli—viral; spirilla—fungal','a','Read carefully: the stem asks about bacterial shape. Identify the keyword: shape. Eliminate wrong answers by matching each classification accurately. Apply safety/procedure logic: correct terminology supports sound infection-control decisions. Make the best remaining choice: cocci are round, bacilli are rod-shaped, and spirilla are spiral-shaped.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-004','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','Certain bacteria encounter unfavorable conditions and shift into a resistant, inactive state. Which interpretation is most accurate?','The bacteria are in an inactive spore-forming stage rather than actively reproducing','The bacteria have become viruses and can no longer return to an active state','The bacteria are undergoing rapid binary fission because conditions are unfavorable','The bacteria have been sterilized and are permanently destroyed','a','Read carefully: the question contrasts unfavorable conditions with active reproduction. Identify the keyword: inactive. Eliminate choices that describe viruses, rapid growth, or sterilization. Apply safety/procedure logic: resistant bacterial spores are associated with an inactive stage, not ordinary active multiplication. Make the best remaining choice: the organism is in an inactive spore-forming state.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-006','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','After cleaning a reusable nonporous implement, which factor should control the barber’s choice of disinfectant?','Whether the product is EPA-registered and labeled for the intended use on that type of item or surface','Whether the product has the strongest odor in the shop','Whether the product is marketed primarily as a skin antiseptic','Whether another shop uses the same color solution','a','Read carefully: the decision is which disinfectant is appropriate after cleaning. Identify the keyword: labeled use. Eliminate odor, color, and skin-antiseptic choices because they do not establish implement-disinfection suitability. Apply safety/procedure logic: product selection must follow registration and label directions for the intended use. Make the best remaining choice: use an appropriately registered product labeled for that item or surface.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-009','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','Two disinfectants are available. One is labeled for the intended barbering surface and lists the required dilution and contact time; the other has a stronger germ-killing claim but does not list that intended use. Which should the barber choose?','The stronger-sounding product, regardless of labeled use','The product whose label supports the intended use and whose directions can be followed exactly','Whichever product dries fastest','Whichever product can be mixed with another disinfectant','b','Read carefully: the comparison is not about marketing strength but appropriate labeled use. Identify the keyword: label. Eliminate choices based on drying speed, mixing, or unsupported claims. Apply safety/procedure logic: disinfectant effectiveness and safe use depend on following the product label for the intended application. Make the best remaining choice: select the product labeled for that use and follow its directions.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-012','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','Which comparison best distinguishes a local infection from a systemic infection?','A local infection is limited to a particular area, while a systemic infection affects the body more broadly','A local infection is always viral, while a systemic infection is always bacterial','A local infection is harmless, while a systemic infection is always fatal','A local infection requires no infection-control precautions, while a systemic infection does','a','Read carefully: the question asks about the scope of infection. Identify the keywords: local and systemic. Eliminate choices that assign a specific organism type, guarantee severity, or remove infection-control responsibilities. Apply safety/procedure logic: location and spread describe the distinction. Make the best remaining choice: local is limited to an area; systemic involves the body more broadly.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-014','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A barber touches a phone with contaminated gloves and then adjusts a clean clipper guard. What is the main problem?','The guard becomes warm','Cross-contamination through touched surfaces','The phone requires sterilization','The haircut automatically ends','b','Contaminated gloves can transfer material between surfaces and equipment.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-017','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','What is the purpose of Standard Precautions?','Use protective measures for potentially infectious blood and certain body fluids','Identify which clients definitely have disease','Replace hand hygiene','Eliminate PPE','a','Standard Precautions do not depend on knowing a person’s infection status.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-019','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A client is accidentally nicked and begins bleeding. What should the barber do first?','Ignore a small cut','Pause the service and begin the required blood-exposure procedure using appropriate precautions','Finish the haircut','Ask another client to help','b','A blood exposure requires pausing the service and following applicable exposure procedures.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-022','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A barber is checking three different requirements: employee workplace-safety rules, disinfectant product registration and label claims, and state licensing/service rules. Which match is most accurate?','OSHA—workplace safety; EPA—disinfectant registration/label claims; state board or agency—licensing and state practice rules','EPA—workplace safety; state board—federal disinfectant registration; OSHA—state licensing','State board—federal workplace law; OSHA—product registration; EPA—license renewal','All three agencies perform the same regulatory function','a','Read carefully: the stem separates three regulatory functions. Identify the keywords: workplace safety, disinfectant registration, and state licensing. Eliminate choices that swap agency roles or treat them as identical. Apply safety/procedure logic: compliance depends on identifying the controlling authority for the issue. Make the best remaining choice: OSHA addresses workplace safety, EPA addresses disinfectant registration and labeled claims, and the state authority governs licensing and state practice rules.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-025','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A worker pours concentrated chemical into an unlabeled container and plans to guess the dilution later. What is the best response?','Proceed if experienced','Add water until odor is mild','Stop and use proper identification plus label/SDS-directed handling and dilution information','Mix in another cleaner','c','Chemical handling depends on correct identification and product-directed safety information, not guessing.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-027','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A barber learned a safety rule years ago, but the state authority has since updated its requirements. What is the barber’s professional responsibility?','Keep using the old rule until an inspector gives a warning','Follow current applicable requirements and stay informed about rule and licensing updates','Use whichever version is easier during a busy day','Ignore state updates if the shop has its own policy','b','Read carefully: the issue is an updated controlling requirement. Identify the keyword: current. Eliminate choices that rely on outdated practice, convenience, or shop policy over applicable rules. Apply safety/procedure logic: professional responsibility includes staying current with licensing and regulatory requirements. Make the best remaining choice: follow the current applicable requirement and keep up with updates.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-4-030','chapter_quiz','4','scientific_concepts','A station is cleaned and disinfected, but a clean cape is placed on a still-contaminated headrest cover. What is the best next action?','Seat the client because the cape is clean','Spray the cape with disinfectant','Correct the contaminated headrest condition before clean client-contact items or the next service','Turn the cover over','c','The relevant client-contact environment must be addressed so clean items are not recontaminated.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-4-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-001','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','A superficial abrasion begins repairing. Which process BEST produces new somatic cells for tissue renewal?','Mitosis','Metabolism','Diffusion','Keratinization','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST. Eliminate wrong answers: metabolism, diffusion, and keratinization do not directly divide one somatic cell into two. Apply safety/procedure logic: choose the process responsible for ordinary growth and repair. Then make the best remaining choice: mitosis.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-005','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','A barber wants to remember why blood is classified differently from skin. Which statement is BEST?','Blood is connective tissue; skin surface is primarily epithelial tissue','Blood is epithelial tissue; skin is nervous tissue','Blood is muscular tissue; skin is connective tissue only','Blood and skin are both organs, not tissues','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST. Eliminate wrong answers: eliminate answers that misclassify major tissue families. Apply safety/procedure logic: classify by tissue type, not by where it is encountered. Then make the best remaining choice: blood is connective tissue and epidermal covering is epithelial.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-010','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which statement BEST explains why physiology matters to safe barbering?','It explains how structures function and respond during services','It allows barbers to diagnose disease','It replaces sanitation rules','It permits medical treatment of skin conditions','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST explains. Eliminate wrong answers: scope-of-practice violations eliminate diagnosis and treatment claims. Apply safety/procedure logic: use physiology to understand normal function without crossing scope. Then make the best remaining choice: physiology supports safer service decisions.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-014','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which statement about the adult spinal column is MOST accurate for this chapter?','It is described as 26 bones because the sacrum and coccyx are fused in adults','It contains only 24 bones total','It contains 33 separate bones in every adult','It excludes the cervical region','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: adult. Eliminate wrong answers: distinguish developmental vertebral segments from adult fused bones. Apply safety/procedure logic: use the adult-anatomy convention in the lesson. Then make the best remaining choice: 26 bones including fused sacrum and coccyx.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-019','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which pairing is CORRECT?','Orbicularis oculi—closes the eyelid','Orbicularis oris—raises the eyebrow','Buccinator—rotates the head','Platysma—closes the jaw as the main chewing muscle','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: CORRECT. Eliminate wrong answers: the distractors mismatch function and muscle. Apply safety/procedure logic: match anatomy to action. Then make the best remaining choice: orbicularis oculi closes the eyelid.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-023','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','A client becomes dizzy during forceful neck work. What is the BEST immediate barber response?','Stop the service, keep the client safely positioned, assess responsiveness/symptoms, and follow first-aid or emergency procedures as needed','Increase pressure to finish the massage','Diagnose vagus-nerve stimulation','Continue if the client says they can tolerate it','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST immediate. Eliminate wrong answers: continuing, increasing pressure, or diagnosing violates safety/scope. Apply safety/procedure logic: stop the provoking service and protect the client first. Then make the best remaining choice: stop, position safely, assess, and escalate appropriately.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-028','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','A question asks which artery supplies the chin and lower-lip region. Which answer is MOST accurate?','Submental artery','Supraorbital artery','Parietal artery','Posterior auricular artery','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: chin and lower lip. Eliminate wrong answers: forehead, crown, and behind-ear vessels do not match the target region. Apply safety/procedure logic: match the named artery to its facial territory. Then make the best remaining choice: submental artery.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-032','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which statement about lymph nodes is MOST accurate?','They filter lymph and support immune activity; swelling can have multiple causes','They pump blood to the scalp','They produce sebum','Any swelling proves infection','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: MOST accurate. Eliminate wrong answers: blood pumping and sebum are unrelated, and swelling is not single-cause proof. Apply safety/procedure logic: avoid diagnostic absolutes. Then make the best remaining choice: filtering and immune support are correct.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-037','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','A barber sees an oily scalp. Which statement is the BEST anatomy-based explanation without overstepping scope?','Sebaceous glands produce sebum that lubricates skin and hair, but oiliness can vary for many reasons','Oiliness proves a hormonal disorder','Sweat glands produce sebum','The epidermis pumps oil into follicles','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST. Eliminate wrong answers: diagnosis is too strong and the other anatomy is wrong. Apply safety/procedure logic: give general anatomy without assigning a disease cause. Then make the best remaining choice: sebaceous glands produce sebum.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-041','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which statement about the pituitary gland is MOST accurate?','It is often called the master gland because its hormones regulate several other endocrine glands, but it does not control every endocrine gland','It directly controls every endocrine gland','It is a sweat gland','It is located in the skin','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: MOST accurate. Eliminate wrong answers: reject the absolute and category errors. Apply safety/procedure logic: use qualified endocrine relationships. Then make the best remaining choice: regulates several, not all, endocrine glands.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-046','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which statement BEST describes the respiratory system’s role in oxygen supply?','It brings oxygen into the body; the cardiovascular system then transports oxygen to tissues','It directly pumps oxygen through arteries','It delivers oxygen only to hair follicles','It replaces cardiovascular circulation','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST describes. Eliminate wrong answers: transport through tissues is cardiovascular, not direct respiratory pumping. Apply safety/procedure logic: separate gas exchange from transport. Then make the best remaining choice: respiration loads oxygen; circulation delivers it.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-6-050','chapter_quiz','6','scientific_concepts','Which statement BEST explains why reproductive-system changes are included in this chapter?','Life-stage hormonal changes can influence hair-growth patterns, texture, and skin condition, with individual variation','They allow barbers to diagnose pregnancy from hair changes','They guarantee identical hair changes in everyone','They replace endocrine-system function','a','Read carefully. Identify the keyword: BEST explains. Eliminate wrong answers: diagnosis, guarantees, and system replacement are incorrect. Apply safety/procedure logic: use association and variation, not certainty. Then make the best remaining choice: life-stage hormones can influence hair and skin.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-6-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-001','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','Which statement best describes organic chemistry in the context of Chapter 7?','It focuses on carbon-containing substances and compounds','It includes only substances that came from living organisms','It includes every product that can burn','It excludes synthetic carbon-containing materials','a','Organic chemistry focuses on carbon-containing substances and compounds. Living-versus-nonliving and flammability are not reliable classification shortcuts.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-005','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A sample contains only one type of atom and cannot be chemically separated into simpler substances. How should it be classified?','Element','Compound','Suspension','Emulsion','a','An element is a basic form of matter made of one type of atom. A compound contains different elements chemically combined.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-010','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A temporary color product mainly deposits color near the hair surface, while an oxidation haircolor develops through a chemical reaction. What concept is being tested?','Physical change versus chemical change','Organic versus inorganic chemistry','Hard water versus soft water','Solution versus suspension','a','Surface deposition can primarily represent a physical change, while oxidation haircolor depends on a chemical reaction. The key is whether chemical composition changes.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-014','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','During permanent waving, which sequence best describes the redox chemistry?','Reduction changes disulfide bonds first; oxidation during neutralization helps reform them in the new shape','Oxidation breaks the bonds first; reduction permanently seals the cuticle','Acid-alkali neutralization breaks and reforms the bonds','No redox reaction is involved if the hair is wrapped on rods','a','The waving phase uses reduction to alter disulfide bonds, followed by oxidation during neutralization to help reform bonds in the new shape.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-019','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A product separates while standing, and its label instructs the barber to redistribute the contents before use. Which mixture behavior is most consistent with that observation?','Suspension-like settling','A pure element changing state','A fixed-composition compound','A neutral pH reaction','a','Suspensions contain dispersed particles that can settle. The product label remains the controlling instruction for whether and how to redistribute the product.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-023','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A student identifies every product labeled “shake well” as a suspension. What is the best correction?','Settling may suggest suspension behavior, but product type should not be identified from one label phrase alone','The student is always correct because only suspensions are shaken','The student is wrong because suspensions never separate','Any product that is shaken must be an emulsion','a','Some suspensions settle and may require redistribution, but a single label phrase is not enough to classify every product. Use the product’s actual formulation and directions.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-028','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A client has persistent mineral buildup associated with hard water. Which chemistry fact most directly explains why a clarifying or chelating cleanser may be considered?','Hard water contains more dissolved minerals that can contribute deposits on hair','Hard water is more acidic than all shampoos','Soft water permanently closes the cuticle','Minerals convert every shampoo into a suspension','a','Hard water contains higher levels of minerals such as calcium and magnesium, which can contribute deposits and affect lather. Product choice should match the actual buildup and client condition.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-032','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A client has noticeable product and mineral buildup but already reports dryness. Which choice best applies product-purpose reasoning?','Consider a clarifying or chelating cleanser for the buildup while avoiding an automatic fixed schedule and supporting the hair’s condition','Use clarifying shampoo every day because buildup is present','Use medicated shampoo because it is stronger','Use any shampoo because all surfactants have the same purpose','a','Clarifying or chelating products may address buildup, but frequency and follow-up should match the client’s hair condition and product directions rather than a fixed schedule.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-037','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','Hair needs brief conditioning after shampooing and the product is designed to be rinsed out shortly after application. Which category best fits?','Instant/rinse-out conditioner','Leave-in conditioner','Dry shampoo','Styling wax','a','An instant or rinse-out conditioner is applied after shampooing, left on briefly according to directions, and then rinsed.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-041','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','Which ingredient-purpose pairing is most defensible?','Glycerin — humectant used to help attract and retain moisture','Alum — surfactant used to emulsify oil and water','Petrolatum — oxidizing agent used to develop haircolor','Witch hazel — reducing agent used to break disulfide bonds','a','Glycerin is commonly used as a humectant. The other pairings assign unrelated chemistry functions.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-046','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A chemical service may require a predisposition, strand, or other pre-service test. How should the barber determine the correct test and timing?','Use the specific product label, manufacturer directions, and applicable rules','Use the same 24-hour patch test for every service','Skip testing whenever the client has used the product before','Choose the test based only on product fragrance','a','Pre-service testing is product- and service-specific. The required method and timing come from the product directions and applicable rules.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-7-050','chapter_quiz','7','scientific_concepts','A client’s hair is already compromised, the service uses an alkaline chemical, and the product directions warn against overprocessing. Which reasoning sequence is best?','Recognize that alkalinity can increase swelling and porosity, assess the hair condition, follow the exact timing/directions, and stop if safety limits are reached','Assume a higher pH guarantees a better result and extend the processing time','Neutralize the product by adding an acid before applying it','Ignore the client’s chemical history because pH alone determines the outcome','a','Safe chemical-service reasoning combines chemistry with client condition and product directions. Alkalinity can increase swelling and porosity, so overprocessing risk must be controlled.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-7-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-001','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','Electricity is classified as energy rather than matter. What does this mean?','It does not occupy space or have mass','It cannot be measured or controlled','It only works in complete darkness','It requires a vacuum to function','a','Electricity is treated as energy rather than matter because it does not occupy space or have mass. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-004','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','Direct current (DC) flows in how many directions?','Two directions, alternating','One direction only','Three directions simultaneously','No direction because it is static','b','Direct current flows in one direction. Batteries are a common source of DC. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-006','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A barber reads the voltage rating on a new electrical tool before plugging it in. What is the BEST reason for checking that rating?','To confirm the tool is compatible with the available electrical supply','To determine whether the tool is automatically grounded','To calculate how often the tool must be disinfected','To determine whether the tool produces direct or alternating current internally','a','Voltage describes electrical potential or pressure. Matching the tool rating to the available supply is the relevant equipment-use decision. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-009','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A school is purchasing new electrical tools. Which choice BEST reflects safe equipment-selection reasoning?','Choose equipment that meets applicable workplace requirements and carries recognized safety certification or listing when required','Choose any tool with the highest wattage because higher power always means greater safety','Choose equipment without a grounding feature because two-prong plugs are easier to use','Choose the least expensive tool because electrical testing is the manufacturer''s responsibility only','a','Recognized certification/listing and applicable workplace requirements are relevant safety indicators. Price or wattage alone does not establish safe suitability. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-012','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A circuit breaker trips twice while the same group of tools is operating. What is the BEST professional response?','Reset it repeatedly until the service is finished','Stop and have the load or equipment condition evaluated before continuing the same setup','Replace the breaker with one that has a higher rating','Remove grounding pins from the highest-wattage tools','b','Repeated tripping is a warning condition. A barber should not defeat protective devices or alter the electrical system to keep working. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-014','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','What is the formula for calculating watts?','Watts = Volts ÷ Amps','Watts = Amps × Volts','Watts = Ohms × Volts','Watts = Amps ÷ Ohms','b','Electrical power in watts can be calculated as volts multiplied by amps. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-017','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A client requests an electrical facial service that the barber has read about but has never been trained to perform. What is the BEST next step?','Proceed at the lowest setting because low intensity removes the training requirement','Proceed if the client signs consent','Do not perform it until scope, training, client screening, and device requirements are satisfied','Use only the positive pole because it is always the safer pole','c','Knowing terminology does not authorize performance. Scope, training, client suitability, and device instructions all matter before service. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-019','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A permitted galvanic cleansing procedure calls for desincrustation. Which statement BEST describes the concept without overstating the result?','It is a source-described alkaline galvanic cleansing process intended to help emulsify sebum and debris','It sterilizes pores and guarantees removal of all bacteria','It is a light-therapy process that converts UV energy into heat','It is a universal pre-service step for every client regardless of device instructions','a','Desincrustation is described as a galvanic cleansing process involving an alkaline reaction. It is not a guaranteed sterilizing treatment or a universal service step. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-022','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A client requests microcurrent after hearing broad cosmetic claims online. What is the BEST professional response before service?','Verify scope, training, client history, device contraindications, and manufacturer instructions','Proceed because very low current means contraindications do not apply','Proceed if the client says they have used a similar device before','Increase intensity until the client can clearly feel the current','a','Low-level current does not remove the need for scope, training, screening, and device-specific safety requirements. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-025','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','Which statement BEST distinguishes UVA, UVB, and UVC for Chapter 8 study?','UVA is associated with tanning/photoaging, UVB with sunburn/skin damage, and UVC with germicidal applications','UVA is germicidal, UVB is visible red light, and UVC is infrared heat','UVA, UVB, and UVC are three names for the same wavelength','Only UVC can affect skin or eyes','a','The source distinguishes the UV bands by wavelength and associated effects/applications. UV exposure can injure skin and eyes. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-027','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','A device uses colored LEDs for a cosmetic service. How should the barber interpret color-based treatment claims?','As device-dependent indications that still require scope, client suitability, and manufacturer verification','As guaranteed medical outcomes that apply to every client','As proof that eye protection is never required','As a reason to ignore medication or photosensitivity screening','a','The source associates LED colors with different purposes, but actual indications and safe use depend on the device, client, and permitted scope. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-8-030','chapter_quiz','8','scientific_concepts','Two professional light devices specify different exposure times, distances, and eye-protection requirements. Which rule should guide the barber?','Use one universal five-minute and 30-inch rule for both devices','Use the operating parameters and protection required for each specific device and procedure while supervising the client continuously','Use the longest exposure from either device so both treatments are effective','Let the client choose the distance and exposure based on comfort alone','b','Different light devices can require different operating parameters. Device-specific instructions, required protection, client screening, and continuous supervision take priority over memorized universal numbers. Strategy: Read carefully, identify the keyword, eliminate wrong answers, apply safety/procedure logic, then choose the best remaining answer.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-8-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active')
